aking it harder to achieve concealed-hand patterns and limiting my scoring potential.\n\n5. Current hand doesn't show strong patterns toward high-scoring combinations. The tiles are mixed suits without clear direction.\n\n**Chi T2 Analysis:**\n- Would give me a meld but further reduce hand flexibility\n- Already have one exposed meld, adding another limits concealed hand bonuses\n- Doesn't significantly improve my path to 8+ points\n\n**Pass Analysis:**\n- Keeps hand concealed (except the one Pung)\n- Maintains flexibility for better tile draws\n- Current hand is too weak; better to wait for more useful tiles\n\nReason: \nMy hand is currently too fragmented and weak to justify exposing another meld. With only [W8, W8, W8] exposed and a scattered hand of pairs and singles, I lack a clear path to 8+ points. Chi-ing T2 would commit me further to an open hand strategy without sufficient scoring potential. It's better to Pass and maintain flexibility, hoping to draw tiles that create better combinations or clearer patterns toward higher-scoring hands like Half Flush, All Pungs, or concealed patterns.\n\nAnswer: Pass"}
